    {
      "page": 1,
      "text": "We organize the experiments around utility, behavioral scope, and lifecycle attribution. Repeated standard-task evaluations of SkillEvolver, SPARK, and CoEvoSkills measure skill utility, and controlled task variants examine how far that utility extends. Inspection of skill content and execution traces then identifies reusable decisions expressed during deployment. Complementary mechanism studies in SkillRevise, SkillHone, and SkillOpt examine retention and the origins of observed gains. These studies represent trace-conditioned revision, history-based iterative honing, and validation-gated bounded editing in frozen-agent systems with persistent external skill artifacts.",
